# "hello" at 115200 baud on channel 0, 1 MSa/s, 8 channels (4 samples a word).
# The start bit falls at sample 1000, so the burst starts pre = 100 earlier.
# The last change is the stop bit of 'o' rising at sample 1425, in word 356;
# the idle scan reports the end of that word, so last_change = 1428.
# The gap is checked at the end of each 1024-sample period: at 2048 the line
# has been quiet 620 samples, at 3072 1644 >= 1000, so the burst ends there,
# keeping post = 200 after the last change.
sample uart_hello.sr
period_words 256
pre 100
post 200
gap 1000
burst 900 1000 1628
